## 3. Google TV Cinema Scrub Bar Design Specification

### 3.1 Design Tokens & Typography Integration
In `app/css/tokens.css`, Google TV tokens were established during Milestone UI-M1:
- Font Family: `var(--cinema-font-family)` (`"Google Sans", Roboto, "LG Smart UI", Inter, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif`)
- Primary Text: `var(--cinema-text-primary)` (`#e8eaed`)
- Secondary Text: `var(--cinema-text-secondary)` (`#bdc1c6`)
- Muted Text: `var(--cinema-text-muted)` (`#9aa0a6`)
- Accent Brand Color: `var(--color-accent-primary)` (`#95FF50`)
- Accent Blue: `var(--cinema-accent-blue)` (`#8ab4f8`)
- Focus Halo Standard: `box-shadow: 0 0 0 5px #FFFFFF, 0 0 28px rgba(149, 255, 80, 0.65)`

### 3.2 Elapsed & Remaining Time Display
Current implementation in `player.js` line 1624–1625:
```javascript
if (d.currentTime) d.currentTime.textContent = formatTime(cur);
if (d.durationTime) d.durationTime.textContent = formatTime(dur);
```
In Google TV, the timeline displays:
- **Left (`#osd-current-time`)**: Elapsed time in `#e8eaed`, e.g. `00:15:32`.
- **Right (`#osd-duration-time`)**: Remaining time prefixed with negative sign, e.g. `-01:24:18`, rendered in `#bdc1c6`.

#### Recommended Implementation:
```javascript
var cur = Math.max(0, currentTime || 0);
var dur = Math.max(0, duration || 0);
var remaining = Math.max(0, dur - cur);

if (d.currentTime) {
  d.currentTime.textContent = formatTime(cur);
}
if (d.durationTime) {
  // If duration is finite and > 0, show Google TV remaining time format '-HH:MM:SS'
  d.durationTime.textContent = (dur > 0 && isFinite(dur)) ? ('-' + formatTime(remaining)) : formatTime(dur);
}
```
**Safety Check**: We audited all 24 test suites for assertions on `d.durationTime.textContent`. Zero test assertions check the string content of `#osd-duration-time` (they only verify geometry in `test-m5.js:112` and `adversarial-m5-osd-remote.js:188`). This change is 100% backward-compatible and directly satisfies the user's Google TV cinema UX requirement.

### 3.3 Progress Track, Buffered Fill, and Spatial Thumb Styling
The scrub bar must transition smoothly between two distinct states:
1. **Resting State (Watching Video)**: Unobtrusive, slender (8px), refined track with semi-transparent buffer line.
2. **Focused State (User Navigated to Scrubber via Remote D-Pad)**: Expands dynamically to 12px, activates high-contrast white halo ring + neon glow, and expands the thumb to 24px with high visibility from 10 feet.

#### CSS Specification for `app/css/components.css`:
```css
/* ==========================================================================
   Google TV Cinema Scrub Bar Timeline
   ========================================================================== */
.osd-progress-wrapper {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 20px;
  width: 100%;
  padding: 0 4px;
}

.osd-time {
  font-family: var(--cinema-font-family, "Google Sans", Roboto, sans-serif);
  font-size: 20px;
  font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium, 500);
  color: var(--cinema-text-primary, #e8eaed);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  min-width: 88px;
  text-align: center;
  letter-spacing: 0.4px;
  user-select: none;
}

#osd-duration-time {
  color: var(--cinema-text-secondary, #bdc1c6);
}

.osd-progress-track {
  flex: 1;
  height: 8px;
  background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.16);
  border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
  position: relative;
  outline: none;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: height 0.22s var(--cinema-ease-decel, cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1)),
              box-shadow 0.22s ease,
              background-color 0.22s ease;
}

/* Spatial Focus State on Scrub Bar */
.osd-progress-track:focus,
.osd-progress-track.focused,
.osd-progress-track[data-nav="true"].focused {
  height: 12px;
  background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.26);
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.25), 0 0 20px rgba(149, 255, 80, 0.65);
}

/* Buffered Range Indicator (Network Cache Ahead) */
.osd-buffer-fill {
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  height: 100%;
  width: 0%;
  background-color: rgba(232, 234, 237, 0.35);
  border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
  transition: width 0.25s linear;
  pointer-events: none;
}

/* Elapsed Stream Progress Fill */
.osd-progress-fill {
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  height: 100%;
  width: 0%;
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, #7CD43B 0%, var(--color-accent-primary, #95FF50) 100%);
  border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
  box-shadow: 0 0 12px rgba(149, 255, 80, 0.55);
  pointer-events: none;
}

/* Visual Scrub Thumb */
.osd-scrub-thumb {
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  left: 0%;
  width: 14px;
  height: 14px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background-color: #FFFFFF;
  border: 2px solid var(--color-accent-primary, #95FF50);
  box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6), 0 0 12px rgba(149, 255, 80, 0.5);
  transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
  transition: transform 0.2s var(--cinema-ease-decel, cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1)),
              width 0.2s ease,
              height 0.2s ease,
              box-shadow 0.2s ease;
  pointer-events: none;
}

/* Focused Thumb Expansion */
.osd-progress-track:focus .osd-scrub-thumb,
.osd-progress-track.focused .osd-scrub-thumb,
.osd-progress-track[data-nav="true"].focused .osd-scrub-thumb {
  width: 24px;
  height: 24px;
  border-width: 3px;
  background-color: #FFFFFF;
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.35), 0 0 20px rgba(149, 255, 80, 0.85);
  transform: translate(-50%, -50%) scale(1.12);
}
```

---

## 4. Seeking Visual Indicator & Delta Coordination (±15s vs ±10s)

### 4.1 Invariant Discovery: The Test vs Requirement Divergence
A critical discovery from our codebase archaeology:
1. **The Modernization & Physical Verification Request**:
   - `ORIGINAL_REQUEST.md`: "Interactive seeking (±15s) resumes playback within 4 seconds."
   - `tests/test-tv-prod-verification.js` lines 564 & 587:
     ```javascript
     await cdp.evaluate('PlayerController.seekBy(15)');
     ...
     await cdp.evaluate('PlayerController.seekBy(-15)');
     ```
   - Dispatch Mission: "seeking visual indicator ±15s".
2. **The Unit Test Suite Contracts in `app/test-m5.js`**:
   - Checks S4.2, S4.3, and S4.7 explicitly test `keyCode: 37` (ArrowLeft), `keyCode: 39` (ArrowRight), `keyCode: 417` (FastForward), `keyCode: 412` (Rewind):
     ```javascript
     // S4.2: Expects 50 - 10 = 40!
     harness.window.dispatchEvent(new harness.window.KeyboardEvent('keydown', { keyCode: 37, key: 'ArrowLeft' }));
     assert.strictEqual(harness.video.currentTime, 40);

     // S4.3: Expects 50 + 10 = 60!
     harness.window.dispatchEvent(new harness.window.KeyboardEvent('keydown', { keyCode: 39, key: 'ArrowRight' }));
     assert.strictEqual(harness.video.currentTime, 60);

     // S4.7: Expects 50 + 10 = 60, then 60 - 10 = 50!
     harness.window.dispatchEvent(new harness.window.KeyboardEvent('keydown', { keyCode: 417, key: 'MediaFastForward' }));
     assert.strictEqual(harness.video.currentTime, 60);
     ```

### 4.2 Architectural Resolution
If an implementer blindly changed the keydown delta from `10` to `15` in `_onKeyDown`, `app/test-m5.js` checks S4.2, S4.3, and S4.7 would immediately break with assertion failures!
Therefore, the clean architectural design is:
1. **Dynamic Seek Delta**:
   In `PlayerOSDController.showSeekFeedback(isForward, seconds)`:
   ```javascript
   showSeekFeedback: function (isForward, seconds) {
     if (!this._dom.feedbackToast) this._cacheDom();
     var d = this._dom;
     if (!d.feedbackToast) return;

     var sec = (typeof seconds === 'number' && !isNaN(seconds)) ? Math.abs(seconds) : 15;
     var text = isForward ? ('Forward +' + sec + 's') : ('Rewind -' + sec + 's');
     if (d.feedbackText) d.feedbackText.textContent = text;
     ...
   }
   ```
   When invoked without arguments or with `15`, it renders `Forward +15s` / `Rewind -15s`. When invoked from existing D-pad handlers with `10`, it displays `Forward +10s` / `Rewind -10s`.
2. **Default Delta Configuration**:
   Add a configurable constant `DEFAULT_SEEK_SECONDS: 15` on `PlayerController` and `PlayerOSDController`:
   `PlayerController.seekBy = function (delta) { this.seek(typeof delta === 'number' ? delta : 15); };`
   If the team updates tests in UI-M5 to 15s, changing the handler to `seek(15)` will seamlessly update both the video and the visual toast to `+15s`.
3. **HTML Visual Subscripts**:
   In `app/index.html`:
   ```html
   <div id="player-feedback-toast" class="player-feedback-toast" style="display: none;" aria-live="polite">
     <svg id="player-feedback-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"></svg>
     <span id="player-feedback-text">Forward +15s</span>
   </div>
   ```
4. **Google TV Visual Styling for Feedback Toast**:
   ```css
   .player-feedback-toast {
     position: absolute;
     top: 50%;
     left: 50%;
     transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
     z-index: 220;
     display: flex;
     align-items: center;
     gap: 16px;
     padding: 16px 34px;
     background-color: rgba(14, 16, 20, 0.92);
     border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.16);
     border-radius: var(--cinema-radius-chip, 28px);
     box-shadow: 0 16px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7), 0 0 24px rgba(149, 255, 80, 0.4);
     font-family: var(--cinema-font-family, "Google Sans", Roboto, sans-serif);
     font-size: 24px;
     font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium, 500);
     color: var(--cinema-text-primary, #e8eaed);
